  "question": {
    "text": "Let the mean and standard deviation of marks of class A of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math>&nbsp;students be respectively <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, and the mean and standard deviation of marks of class <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> students be respectively <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>55</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></math>. If the mean and variance of the marks of the combined class of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></math> students are respectively <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>350</mn></math> , then the sum of variances of classes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
